# Linux Day 2 Practice

Today I practiced additional Linux file handling commands in Ubuntu terminal.

## Commands Practiced

### 1. cat

Used to display the content of a file.

### 2. cp

Used to copy files from one location to another.

### 3. mv

Used to move or rename files and directories.

### 4. rm

Used to remove/delete files.

### 5. clear

Used to clear the terminal screen.

## Outcome

Learned basic file management operations such as viewing, copying, renaming, deleting files, and managing terminal workspace in Linux.
